# A record whose head is a reference place to an ordinary Structure launches that Structure by the same two forms (R22,
# item 2; plan M11 5b): a record on a place head is never a declaration, so the root executes it now, as a callable's
# code does -- `p()` runs Model over itself, `q(main\data\D)` and `q(data := main\data\D)` run Add over D.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the reference places p and q stay
# at the root and point into that data by path (a reference declaration in a data part is not executed yet). The dump
# of the root prints main as written, so the places model_v and d_v hold what the dump of Model and D showed (3, 20).
# The code of main is a bare `return`: a method with one parenthesized part and no code reads that part as its code.
sub: main () (
    Model:
        int: v 1
        v := v + 1
    Add:
        v := v + 10
    D:
        int: v 0
)
    return
main()
@: p main\data\Model
@: q main\data\Add
p()
q(main\data\D)
fn: f () int
    p()
    q(data := main\data\D)
    return: main\data\Model\v * 100 + main\data\D\v
int: seen f()
int: model_v main\data\Model\v
int: d_v main\data\D\v
